# KSV014 / readOnlyRootFilesystem: The frontend (Nuxt/Nitro) writes temporary
# files to the container filesystem at runtime. The container runs as non-root
# with all capabilities dropped and seccomp RuntimeDefault applied.
KSV014

# AVD-KSV-01010 / sensitive ConfigMap keys: NITRO_PORT is a TCP port number,
# not a secret. Trivy's heuristic false-positives on the "PORT" substring.
AVD-KSV-01010

# GO-2026-5932 / golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp unmaintained: golang.org/x/crypto
# is an indirect dependency only; no code imports openpgp (or any x/crypto
# subpackage). No fixed version exists — the package is permanently deprecated.
GO-2026-5932

# GHSA-cp6q-959q-f8rh / @tiptap/core mergeAttributes prototype pollution:
# tiptap is only pulled in as an unmet optional peer of @nuxt/ui, itself a
# transitive dep of the nuxt-site-config devtools layer (from @nuxtjs/sitemap
# and @nuxtjs/robots). No app code imports @tiptap or renders a rich-text
# editor, so the vulnerable mergeAttributes() path is never reached. Bumping
# it clean requires forcing pnpm to re-resolve the whole @nuxt/ui peer tree,
# which rewrites most of pnpm-lock.yaml for a package that isn't used.
GHSA-cp6q-959q-f8rh
